<title>UK: BoE confirms will auction gilts due 2007 in June.</title>
<headline>BoE confirms will auction gilts due 2007 in June.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England confirmed on Tuesday that its June auction stock will be the 7.25 percent gilt due 2007.</p>
<p>Previously, the Bank had said the June auction details were subject to confirmation following the general election.</p>
<p>&quot;The date of the auction will be confirmed when the date of the budget is known,&quot; the Bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown has pledged to hold a budget within two months of the May 1 elections.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
